# Read by scripts/check-noir.sh. Round circuits (bin packages under this
# directory) in round order, then the libraries whose tests it runs.
CIRCUITS="amm_swap_total"
LIBS="amm_total"
# The total circuits, linted by total-lint. amm_swap_total is the one
# round here and it is total, so it is listed; a round that keeps asserts
# (a seed or init) is left out.
TOTAL_CIRCUITS="amm_swap_total"
# Co-noir entries: the total circuits above call only total-noir entries whose
# hints co-noir runs (to_u64_or, add_or, mul_div_or through amm_total;
# total-noir's page "co-noir compatibility of the library's hints"), because
# the network extends their witnesses in co-noir, whose Brillig VM at the
# pinned co-snarks rev has no integer shift, mask or ConditionalMov.
# check-noir runs total-lint --brillig-ops on every circuit in CIRCUITS and
# fails on any unsupported op, but it does not run co-noir: after a change,
# also run a co-noir witness extension (the e2e, or the flow of total-noir's
# scripts/mpc-check.sh). Required inside the co-SNARK.
# No extra --lib-src (TOTAL_LIB_SRC): amm_total's swap_total calls only total
# entries, whose hints are whitelisted by total's src, and adds no hint of its
# own; the only reported items are std's (the scalar decomposition in
# pss_core's npk_app_hash), justified by pss_core's markers
# (scripts/check-noir.sh counts them). Adding amm_total/src/ here would
# whitelist its hints unreviewed; it has none, so it stays out.
